-SM64 Pocket performance snapshot P1 -- 2026-10-03
+SM64 P2: measure the renderer on your Pocket
 
-The previous optimization has not produced a noticeable improvement in the
-first world on your Pocket. Its simulated CPU savings are not a measured
-whole-game speedup. This build adds measurements to find the actual limit.
-The os30 bitstream, OS, game logic, audio and rendering quality are unchanged.
+Play Bob-omb Battlefield and hold the same slow view for at least five seconds
+with the panel hidden. Press Select+L+R together to show the last completed
+two-second snapshot. Photograph/capture it. The same chord closes the panel.
+The saved numbers remain frozen while visible, excluding the panel's own cost.
 
-TEST
-1. From the SM64 repository, run: make copy
-2. Enter Bob-omb Battlefield and move to a view that feels slow/choppy.
-3. Keep that view for at least five seconds, with the panel closed.
-4. Press Select + L + R together, then release them. You should see
-   "PERF P1 SNAPSHOT". Send a photo of the panel and describe the location.
-5. The same combination closes the panel. After closing it, wait five seconds
-   before taking another sample. A second sample facing a simple view or the
-   sky is useful for comparison, but the slow view is the priority.
+FPS / LCD: rendered frames and actual presentations per second, over all frames.
+GAME / AUD: game logic and audio preparation, milliseconds per rendered frame.
+REND / WAIT: rendering and frame acquisition, milliseconds per rendered frame.
 
-The values come from the last complete two-second window BEFORE opening the
-panel. They stay frozen. The game continues behind the panel, and drawing the
-panel can slow it down; that extra work is excluded from the saved values.
-If there is no valid sample yet, close the panel, play five seconds, and reopen.
+The next four lines sample one rendered frame in eight. All numbers are ms:
+DL: display-list interpretation and state commands.
+VERT: matrix/vertex loads and deferred texture-coordinate/lighting evaluation.
+TRI: CPU triangle preparation, visibility/culling, clipping and batching.
+MAT: combiner/material selection and renderer-state preparation.
+TILE: texture lookup, conversion, allocation and SDRAM upload/publication.
+SEND: GPU backend conversion, command packing, MMIO uploads and ring stalls.
+SYNC: GPU drain before reusing an in-flight texture buffer (including submit).
+MISC: remaining frame setup and completion work.
+Nested work belongs to only one bucket. SEND is CPU wall time, not GPU busy time.
+SMP: number of sampled frames. SUM: sampled render time, excluding acquisition.
+The eight buckets add to SUM apart from 0.1ms display truncation. SUM can differ
+from REND because REND includes all frames. Hold a steady view for comparison.
+RING is the all-frame average number of ring polling iterations. Zero does not
+rule out slow MMIO. GEO 1 means the geometry path is enabled, not utilization.
 
-READOUT
-FPS: rendered frames per second. LCD: newly presented frames per second,
-  excluding repeated scans of the same frame. These are window averages.
-SIM: game simulation steps per second. SM64 aims for 30 simulation steps and
-  may skip rendering some steps to catch up; movement speed alone is not FPS.
-GAME: game logic and display-list construction, in milliseconds per rendered
-  frame. Includes any catch-up simulation steps in the measurement window.
-AUD: audio sequence/sample preparation, in ms per rendered frame.
-RENDER: display-list translation and command submission, in ms per rendered
-  frame, excluding WAIT. GPU command-ring stalls are included here.
-WAIT: time waiting for the previous GPU flip fence / a free draw buffer, in
-  ms per rendered frame. GPU execution and display scheduling can both matter.
-GAP: remaining wall time, in ms per rendered frame, outside the measured game,
-  renderer, audio and end-frame work. Includes pacing and loop/service overhead;
-  this is not a pure CPU-idle measurement.
-RING: command-ring polling iterations per rendered frame, not milliseconds.
-GEO: whether the geometry accelerator is enabled (expected 1).
-VERT / TRI: average accelerated input vertices / submitted geometry triangles.
-CPU: runtime-reported CPU clock in MHz, not a fitted timing/Fmax measurement.
+This is a diagnostic build. It adds approximately 3.3-4.3% modeled CPU cost over
+P1 in the first-level test; actual hardware overhead is unmeasured. PERF_DIAG=0
+removes the panel and probes completely for normal performance testing.
 
-COLLECTION COST AND CHECKS
-Six coarse timer reads per simulation/rendered step and existing GPU counters;
-no per-triangle instrumentation, live text, or UART output while collecting.
-The CPU model estimates under 1% overhead in six Bob-omb windows. Actual Pocket
-overhead is not measured. Eight sampled framebuffer/depth pairs match the
-current renderer exactly with the panel hidden. The disabled build matches
-the baseline's per-frame modeled CPU cycles across the full 721-frame route.
-Timing arithmetic, catch-up steps, timer wrap and frozen snapshots are tested.
-This does not yet measure individual LCD frame intervals or prove a speedup.
+This client uses SDRAM textures, not CRAM1/PSRAM textures.
 
